Subject: Restore bar item window order after clicks

Clicking a floating bar can raise its background above the item windows,
obscuring icons and labels while their data and callbacks keep working.
Restore the item order after mouse-up, including empty-background clicks.

Related upstream report (macOS 27; identical root cause not confirmed):
https://github.com/FelixKratz/SketchyBar/issues/850#issuecomment-5712106829

TODO: Remove once an upstream fix is available and verified locally with
item and empty-background clicks on both displays.

diff --git a/src/event.c b/src/event.c
--- a/src/event.c
+++ b/src/event.c
@@ -105,3 +105,9 @@ static void event_mouse_up(void* context) {
   if (bar_item && bar_item->needs_update)
     bar_manager_refresh(&g_bar_manager, false);
+
+  // WindowServer may raise a clicked background above its item windows.
+  // This also handles background clicks with no item update or callback.
+  for (int i = 0; i < g_bar_manager.bar_count; i++) {
+    bar_order_item_windows(g_bar_manager.bars[i]);
+  }
 }
